Cyclic DMA support and other changes.

- changes to support DMA_CYCLIC for MEM_TO_DEV (no DEV_TO_MEM yet).
- Tested with I2S and DAC, with 'speaker-test' or with 'fbdoom'.
- 'dmatest' should still work for normal transfers but *NOT INTERLEAVED*
  with Cyclic DMA running. This is a LIMITATION that will be fixed later.
- Overall Cyclic DMA setup:
    - cyclic descriptors are chained in a loop and processing continues
      forever by default. Periods are split in transfers according to 
      hardware buffering limitations.
    - cyclic descriptor requests interrupt on every completion and prevent
      the descriptors being written by hardware
    - special care for cyclic->non-cyclic transitions
    - stopping cyclic transfers needs specific operation, might need
      some time and it's not synchronous
- descriptor flags
    - Descriptors sent to hardware should include src and dst protocol
    - deburst bit used to split transfers into smaller chunks
    - preserve bit used to prevent descriptor being written by hardware
      on completion
- STOP logic with cyclic control register to stop cyclic transfers
- transfers for cyclic descriptors were eventually reduced in size not to
  starve VGA requests (underrun) which are more hard realtime. To be reviewed
  later
- Many callbacks needed different cyclic/non-cyclic implementations
- Bugfix on channel termination of not yet submitted channels
- Some general cleanup included

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Juan Schroeder <jcschroeder@gmail.com>

